# CI protocol example

Classification: regression. This checks the integer square identity on the
explicit 289-pair domain `[-8,8] x [-8,8]`, plus a false-identity control.
It exercises the package protocol and proves no Erdős-99 claim.
The infinite-domain identity and all canonical theorem certificates are outside
this package's verification claim. No historical artifacts need conversion.

From a clean committed checkout, change this package on a branch and run:

```sh
python3 tools/local_ci.py --base-ref main --integrity --replay --output /tmp/e99-example
```

Use Python 3.14 and bubblewrap on Linux. Only declared inputs are exposed to the
verifier. See `docs/ci/LOCALIZED_CI.md` for the manifest contract and limits.
The remaining question is whether the protocol captures a future package's
actual scientific domain; that requires review of that package.
